                    <death when="1849"/>
                    <occupation>opera singer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Madame Angelica Catalani was a renowned opera singer who made her first appearance in London in 1806, 
    when Robert Dighton published a portrait of her in Semiramide (National Portrait Gallery).  She retired from the stage in 1831.
    Godwin mentions her name cryptically in 1810 - perhaps as a topic of conversation; perhaps as an adv meeting. He records 
    meeting her in 1822, probably with <persName key="YAN02">Mrs Yaniewicz</persName>, and he writes to her in 1824.    
  </p>
                    </note>
